Kind: ablation
Issue: #750
Takes out: trace_frame()'s refusal to walk a frame from ring 3 -- a processor parked in a task's code has its rbp, a register the program uses as it likes, walked as the kernel's chain again; since the step refuses a user address the walk stops at the first frame, so the report says nothing of the ring, and ddb-report-check.sh asks for that line
Script: scripts/ddb-report-boot.sh
Over: 750-widen-task-thread-parked-in-ring-3.patch
Expect: ddb-report-check: WRONG

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/ddb.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/ddb.c
index b37db3bb..1bff5373 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/ddb.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/ddb.c
@@ -373,11 +373,6 @@ static void trace(uint64_t rbp)
  */
 static void trace_frame(const struct trap_frame *f)
 {
-	if ((f->cs & 3) != 0) {
-		cons_puts("  in ring 3: its rbp is the task's and is not walked — "
-			  "resolve rip against the program, not the kernel\r\n");
-		return;
-	}
 	trace(f->rbp);
 }
 
